ally sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm smooth lined cyst filled with thick tan opaque fluid  which is located at approximately 6 o clock  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is unremarkable fibroadipose tissue with focal fibrocystic changes  The fibrocystic changes are most visible in a region around the cystic structure  The cyst is 1cm from the posterior margin  and 2cm from the anterior margin  10 representative sections are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   from lateral to medial  with representative sections of the cyst as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh  labeled  right breast   is a 530 gram  21 x 16 x 2 8cm right simple mastectomy specimen oriented with a stitch marking the axillary tail  On the anterior surface  there is a 4 x 4 5cm skin ellipse containing a 1cm in diameter x 0 5cm tall nipple  The anterior surface of the specimen is inked blue  and the posterior black  and the specimen serially sectioned  There is a poorly defined REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm prior biopsy site with surrounding fibrosis located in the upper outer quadrant of the breast  1 5cm from the posterior margin  and 1 5cm from the anterior margin  No lymph nodes identified in the axillary tail  The remainder of the parenchyma is unremarkable with fibrocystic changes throughout  Sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Sections around prior biopsy scar   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   2 representative sections of breast away from biopsy site  including anterior and posterior margins  Received in formalin  labeled  left mastectomy flap   are 4 fragments of skin aggregating to 4 x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm  Representative sections are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  right mastectomy flap   are multiple fragments of skin aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  Representative sections are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  left sentinel node   is a REMOVED_DATE x 