 2cm medial inferior to the scar  8cm inferior to nodule one  0 7cm from the anterior margin  and 1 0cm from the posterior margin located 6cm inferior to the scar is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm firm  yellow tan area consistent with fat necrosis 0 4cm from the posterior margin  The remaining uninvolved breast tissue is firm  white  and focally cystic  A section of the upper outer quadrant reveals 1 possible lymph node measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodule 1 in its entirety   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodule 2 in its entirety   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Scar in its entirety   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Possible fat necrosis to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved tissue from lower inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved tissue from mid lower quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved tissue from lower outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved tissue from upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 possible lymph node  Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   Breast  Right   Simple Mastectomy  report_end  , Negative.
